    "overall_rainfall_association_significant_after_adjustment": true,
    "final_finding": "Across the analyzed Jharkhand SMAP record, no statistically significant long-term monotonic soil-moisture decline was detected. The state-level trend was slightly negative but highly non-significant, and none of the 984 SMAP cells had a statistically significant long-term trend in the first-pass cell analysis. Seasonal analysis also found no significant state-level seasonal trends, while the seven raw significant cell-season results disappeared after Benjamini-Hochberg FDR correction, leaving no statistically robust spatial-seasonal hotspots. At the same time, the record contains widespread episodic soil-moisture extremes. Soil-moisture and rainfall anomalies show a strong positive same-month association, and that overall association remains significant after an autocorrelation-aware effective-sample-size adjustment. The spatial rainfall relationship is also consistently positive across the mapped SMAP cells and remains stable when the analysis is restricted to closer SMAP-GPM matches. Together, the evidence supports strong rainfall-linked variability and episodic extremes, rather than a simple state-wide long-term drying claim.",
    "causality_statement": "The analyses demonstrate association, not causality."
  },
  "LIMITATIONS": [
    "The primary long-term SMAP trend test is a first-pass Kendall/Mann-Kendall-style analysis and is not a fully seasonality- and autocorrelation-corrected trend model.",
    "The seasonal trend analysis explicitly states that it is not an autocorrelation-corrected Seasonal Mann-Kendall implementation.",
    "Seasonal rainfall-soil-moisture analyses use relatively small complete season-year sample sizes; therefore seasonal estimates should be interpreted cautiously.",
    "The GPM comparison period ends in September 2025, whereas the SMAP analysis continues through September 2026.",
    "The spatial cross-variable analysis maps 984 SMAP cells to 703 coarser GPM cells, so the 984 spatial correlations are not 984 independent spatial experiments.",
    "FDR significance in the spatial cross-variable analysis is a multiple-testing screening result and does not remove all spatial-dependence concerns.",
    "Extreme-event thresholds and the minimum 5 percent affected-cell criterion are analytical definitions used by this study.",
    "Correlation and lagged association establish statistical association, not physical causality."
